    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (3/3 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, region-validated `postcode` field for owners, following the codebase's existing conventions (dedicated validator component \u2192 domain exception \u2192 `@ControllerAdvice` handler, mirroring how telephone/email are handled).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Regions.java`** (new) \u2014 Extracted the city\u2192region lookup (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD; else `UNKNOWN`) into a single shared source of truth.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `postcode` field with `@Column`, getter/setter, and refactored `getLocality()` to delegate to `Regions.regionOf(...)` (removing the now-duplicated private table) so both locality and postcode validation reuse one table.\n\n3. **`rest/validation/PostcodeValidator.java`** (new) \u2014 Single-responsibility validator: accepts an absent postcode; requires 4 digits when present; and when the city maps to a known region, enforces that region's inclusive range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit code.\n\n4. **`rest/error/InvalidPostcodeException.java`** (new) \u2014 Mirrors `InvalidTelephoneException`/`InvalidEmailException`, carrying the rejected value.\n\n5. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 Added a handler returning **400** with `errors: [\"postcode\"]`.\n\n6. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Injected `PostcodeValidator` and invoke it during `addOwner` (right after the required-fields check, since it depends on the validated `city`).\n\n7. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `postcode` to the editable `OwnerFields` schema (so it's part of the request/response DTOs, backward-compatible/optional, mapped automatically by MapStruct and stored/returned).\n\n8. **DB schemas** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 Added the `postcode` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe postcode is validated only when present, so owners created without one remain accepted \u2014 the request contract stays backward-compatible.",
